.TH "PB-ENV-VAULT-UNLOCK" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-vault-unlock - Unlock this account's ENV vault on this machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env vault unlock [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlock this account's ENV vault on this machine

.PP
Unlock encrypted local custody with the password supplied interactively, by stdin, or from a private file. No ENV value is printed by unlocking.

.PP
The local vault protects ENV key custody with a password and optional recovery code. Locking clears unlocked keys from this machine; removing local custody differs from resetting and deleting account values. Never place a password or recovery code in shell arguments.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unlock

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--password-file\fP=""
	read the raw master password from an absolute owner-only file

.PP
\fB--password-stdin\fP[=false]
	read the raw master password from non-interactive stdin


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-vault(1)\fP
